.TH DEBARRASSE 1 "2026-08-04" "senechal" "bashified verb"
.SH NAME
debarrasse \- clear real clutter off $HOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B debarrasse scan
.br
.B debarrasse quarantine
.br
.B debarrasse verify
.br
.B debarrasse purge
.br
.B debarrasse list
.br
.B debarrasse
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B debarrasse
clears real clutter \- stray caches, old installers already installed \-
off the home directory it runs in, without ever deleting a live file
directly. It never trusts a guess about what is safe to lose; it trusts
two independent checks, both of which must pass before anything moves.
.SS The two gates
.TP
.B the hardlink guard
Every file inside a candidate must have \fIst_nlink\fR == 1. Anything
that trips it gets an independent
.BR find (1)
.B \-samefile
sweep over the configured search roots, so the refusal names the
sibling path it is linked from instead of just refusing.
.TP
.B recoverability
Either the candidate matches a declared \(lqregenerable\(rq pattern
(caches, \fB__pycache__\fR \- expected to regenerate, not be restored),
or
.BR garde (1)
confirms an off\-machine copy exists. Real content with no backup and no
regenerable classification is left alone and reported as such, never
quarantined on a guess.
.SS Quarantine, not deletion
.B quarantine
only ever moves a candidate that cleared both gates into
.IR quarantine_root ,
recorded in a manifest with its content hash. That move is what
.B \-n
dry\-runs: with it, \fBquarantine\fR reports exactly what \fBscan\fR
reports and touches nothing.
.PP
.B purge
is the one place this utility can lose data \- it deletes quarantined
items once they are older than \fIpurge_after_days\fR, re\-checking each
one's hash against the manifest first and skipping anything that
changed since it was quarantined. Refused by default, the same shape
.BR installe (1)
uses for its own unowned\-entry guard: \fB\-\-force\fR takes the decision
back, and the point is that it is \fItaken\fR, not defaulted into.
.SS Configuration
Every threshold \- \fIquarantine_root\fR, \fIpurge_after_days\fR,
\fIexclude\fR, the regenerable patterns, the stale\-download extensions
\- is read from \fBsenechal.json\fR's \fBdeclutter\fR block on
.BR main ,
never retyped here. See \fBsenechal.json.example\fR for the full schema
and its rationale.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Report every candidate and its gate verdict. Touches nothing.
.TP
.B quarantine
Move every candidate that cleared both gates into quarantine.
With \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, behaves exactly like \fBscan\fR.
.TP
.B verify
Non\-mutating: manifest integrity (has anything in quarantine been
tampered with or vanished outside this tool?) and which items are past
their purge grace period.
.TP
.B purge
Delete quarantined items past \fIpurge_after_days\fR. Refused without
\fB\-\-force\fR.
.TP
.B list
Print the subcommand table.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
On \fBquarantine\fR, report what would move; move nothing. No effect on
\fBscan\fR or \fBverify\fR, which never write regardless.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Required by \fBpurge\fR, the sole irreversible subcommand. Refused
without it.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Not yet implemented by any subcommand; using it exits \fB4\fR (GAP).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Results on standard output, commentary suppressed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Usage summary, including the exit vocabulary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the utility name and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
kept \- the subcommand's promise was fulfilled (including \(lqzero
candidates, zero problems\(rq \- that is a real, correct answer, not a
no\-op).
.TP
.B 2
usage error \- unknown subcommand or flag.
.TP
.B 4
GAP \- \fB\-\-json\fR was requested and no subcommand implements it yet.
.TP
.B 5
BROKEN \- the underlying Python exited with a code its own contract does
not define; treat as a real bug in \fBdebarrasse\fR or its
implementation, not a finding about the estate.
.TP
.B 6
BLIND \- could not read its domain (no quarantine directory yet on
\fBverify\fR, or \fBsenechal.json\fR's \fBdeclutter\fR block is
unconfigured).
.TP
.B 7
REFUSED \- \fBpurge\fR was called without \fB\-\-force\fR. Re\-run with
it to lift the refusal.
.TP
.B 8
FOUND \- \fBverify\fR found a real problem: something in quarantine was
tampered with or vanished outside this tool.
.TP
.B 9
WARN \- \fBverify\fR found items past their purge grace period. Nothing
is broken; something is waiting on a decision.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEBARRASSE_LEGACY_ROOT
Where the real implementation
(\fItools/home-declutter.py\fR) lives. Defaults to senechal's own
checkout. Overridable for testing against a sandboxed root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR garde (1),
.BR fauche (1),
.BR installe (1)
.PP
\fBCONTRACT.md\fR in this tree, for the promise this page is judged
against. \fBhome-declutter.py\fR's own module docstring, for why the two
gates are independent rather than one check twice.
